I left out both operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0`. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and calling `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich` would need filesystem and HTTP authority (such as `http-client`), which this node doesn't hold. Sending the input's text to an outside service would also go beyond the node's scope. If you want either, the graph's `with` clause has to grant the matching capability first.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{moderated-query, conversation-context};

    import aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(query: moderated-query) -> conversation-context;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::kb_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(query: ModeratedQuery) -> ConversationContext {
        let q = query.query;
        let knowledge = kb_read::lookup(&q.question);
        ConversationContext {
            intent: q.intent,
            question: q.question,
            knowledge,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

